  "body": "Found by the release QA swarm (#2582) on **v0.24.0**, driven through `camcraft-cli mcp` by a Codex agent. Part: plate with a Ø5.0 pilot 10 mm deep (for an M6 tap), Tormach 770MX.\n\n## What happens\nA spot operation (cycle `spot`) with a **Ø6, 120° point** drill, 1 mm deep (entry_z 12, floor_z 11) on 5 hole centres is refused:\n\n```\nmove 11 cuts past the finish surface\npost: post blocked - 1 warning(s): Spot5: move 11 cuts past the finish surface\n```\nAt 1 mm point depth a 120° tip cuts a radius of tan(60°) x 1 = 1.73 mm, inside the 2.5 mm radius of the Ø5 bore, so nothing past the finish surface is cut. The stock sim reports 0 gouge. Changing only the tool diameter to 4 makes the same op verify and post. It looks like the check sweeps the nominal Ø6 cylinder, not the cone that actually enters (compare #266 for taps).\n\n## Expected\nA shallow spot whose cone stays inside the hole is not a gouge.\n\n## Reproduce\nOn skull: `/home/mikekinney/qa/runs/20261120-q01-2d-plate/q01-spot-refusal.camproj` -> `open_project`, `generate {}`, `verify {name:\"Spot5\"}`. Calls: `/home/mikekinney/qa/runs/20261120-q01-2d-plate/evidence.jsonl` steps 94-106; `/home/mikekinney/qa/runs/20261120-q01-2d-plate/REPORT.md` (P3).\n\nNot checked on current main. False refusal (safe direction), but it pushes users to swap tools.\n\nDone means: a spot drill whose cone at the programmed depth stays within the hole's finish surface verifies, pinned by a test; a spot that really enlarges the hole is still refused.\n",
